# 9\. ATTACHMENTS, COMMUNICATIONS, AND INTEGRATIONS

## Attachments

Documents and images must be linked to their correct business records.

Examples include:

- Customer location images.
- Supplier quotations.
- Customer purchase orders.
- Product documents.
- Preparation photographs.
- Sticker evidence.
- Signed delivery documents.
- Invoices and other approved financial documents.

Use appropriate private storage, access controls, file validation, and retention rules.

Never expose sensitive files through unrestricted public URLs.

## Email and WhatsApp Business

Communication integrations must support:

- Approved message templates.
- Recipient selection according to business rules.
- Appropriate document attachments or secure links.
- Message status tracking.
- Failure visibility and retry handling.
- Audit history linking messages to customers and transactions.
- Protection against duplicate sends where required.

Use supported provider APIs and approved credentials.

Do not claim that an email or WhatsApp message was delivered merely because an internal job was queued.

Distinguish queued, sent, accepted by provider, delivered, failed, and other provider-supported states.

Do not assume that email threading, replies, read receipts, GPS tracking, or other external features are available without confirming provider capabilities.

## GPS and external drivers

GPS tracking must be implemented only when the required provider, permissions, device capabilities, privacy rules, and operating conditions are established.

For external drivers, use an approved sharing or delivery workflow appropriate to their access level.

