# 10\. REPORTING AND DATA CONSISTENCY

Dashboards and reports must derive their values from authoritative business records.

Examples include:

- Sales activity and quotation status.
- Purchase orders and remaining quantities.
- Inventory availability and movement history.
- Warehouse preparation and delivery progress.
- Delivered and invoiced quantities.
- Outstanding invoices and overdue balances.
- Partial and completed collections.
- Customer account statements.
- Outstanding approvals and operational tasks.

For every report, define:

- The data source.
- Filters and date boundaries.
- Included document statuses.
- Calculation rules.
- Timezone and currency assumptions.
- Authorization scope.
- Treatment of cancellations and corrections.

Reports must reconcile with underlying records.

Do not independently calculate the same business metric differently across dashboards, exports, and account statements.

Generate scheduled reports only when the reporting requirements, schedule, recipients, and failure behavior are defined.

