# 12\. STANDARD WORKFLOW FOR ALL AGENTS

Every substantial task must follow this sequence.

## Step 1 — Inspect

Read these guidelines, relevant agent rules, repository structure, existing implementation, and tests.

## Step 2 — Identify scope

Determine the module, business workflow, dependencies, affected entities, permissions, and acceptance criteria.

## Step 3 — Check dependencies

Confirm that prerequisite modules and business decisions are available.

Do not build on an unapproved assumption merely to move faster.

## Step 4 — Plan

Identify intended file changes, database impact, security requirements, tests, and potential regressions.

Keep plans proportionate to task complexity.

## Step 5 — Implement or assess

Make only the changes required by the task.

Preserve existing work and avoid unrelated refactoring.

## Step 6 — Test

Run relevant tests and checks. Add regression tests where appropriate.

Test permissions, business invariants, invalid transitions, failure behavior, and edge cases according to risk.

## Step 7 — Review

Review the final diff, migrations, business calculations, authorization, side effects, and compatibility.

## Step 8 — Report

Summarize what changed, what was verified, what remains unresolved, and whether the phase acceptance criteria are satisfied.

