Maintain project documentation as implementation evolves.

At minimum, keep relevant documentation for:

- Business requirements and unresolved decisions.
- Domain terminology and entity relationships.
- Module responsibilities and boundaries.
- Role and permission matrix.
- Document state machines and transitions.
- Pricing, inventory, delivery, and financial invariants.
- API contracts and external integrations.
- Migration and deployment considerations.
- Testing strategy and acceptance criteria.
- Known limitations and technical debt.

Update documentation when approved behavior changes.

Avoid creating duplicate documents that disagree with one another. Identify a clear authoritative location for each category of information.

